<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-align: justify; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B><IMG SRC="ex10-1_001.jpg" ALT=""></B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-align: justify; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 1in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>(b) Total
Disability. </B>The Company may terminate the employment of the Employee immediately upon written notice to the Employee in the event
of the Disability (as that term is hereinafter defined) of the Employee, in which event, the Company shall not have any further obligation
or liability under this Agreement except that the Company shall pay to the Employee: (i) any portion of the Employee&rsquo;s Base Salary
for the period up to the date of termination that has been earned but remains unpaid; (ii) any bonus pursuant to Section 3(b) which has
been earned but not yet paid; and (iii) any benefits that have accrued to the Employee under the terms of the employee benefit plans
of the Company, which benefits shall be paid in accordance with the terms of those plans. For purposes of this Agreement, the term &ldquo;Disability&rdquo;
shall mean an illness, incapacity or a mental or physical condition that renders the Employee unable or incompetent to carry out the
job responsibilities that the Employee held or the tasks that the Employee was assigned at the time the disability commenced for 120
consecutive days or 180 days in a one-year period, as determined by the Board and supported by the opinion of a physician. The Employee
shall fully cooperate with the physician retained to furnish such opinion, including submitting to such examinations and tests as may
be requested by the physician.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 1in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 1in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>(c) Termination
by the Company for Cause. </B>The Company may terminate the Employee&rsquo;s employment hereunder and this Agreement immediately (unless
stated otherwise) upon written notice to the Employee for &ldquo;Cause.&rdquo; For purposes of this Agreement, Cause shall be defined
as: (i) the Employee&rsquo;s material violation of the Company&rsquo;s written policies; (ii) the Employee&rsquo;s willful misconduct
or willful failure to perform the Employee&rsquo;s duties, which continues after ten (10) business days following written notice describing
such failure in reasonable detail; (iii) the Employee&rsquo;s conviction of, plea of guilty or nolo contendere to, a felony or any crime
involving fraud, embezzlement, or moral turpitude; (iv) the Employee&rsquo;s material breach of Sections 5 or 6 of this Agreement; (v)
the Employee&rsquo;s repeated intoxication or use of illegal drugs during working hours after written notice; (vi) the Employee&rsquo;s
gross negligence in the performance of duties which materially harms the Company. No act or omission shall be &ldquo;willful&rdquo; unless
done in bad faith or without reasonable belief that the action or omission was in the best interest of the Company; or (vii) the Employee&rsquo;s
material breach of the Employee&rsquo;s fiduciary duties or material failure to perform or comply with the Employee&rsquo;s corporate
governance responsibilities, including compliance with the Company&rsquo;s Certificate of Incorporation, Bylaws, Code of Business Conduct
and Ethics, insider trading policy, disclosure controls, Board-approved policies, lawful directives of the Board of Directors or any
committee thereof, or applicable securities laws or stock exchange governance requirements, which breach, if capable of cure, is not
cured within ten (10) business days after notice specifying the breach in reasonable detail. For the avoidance of doubt, &ldquo;Cause&rdquo;
shall not mean a failure to achieve scientific goals, financial goals or forecasted timelines. In the event that the Company shall discharge
the Employee pursuant to this Section 4(c), the Company shall not have any further obligation or liability under this Agreement, except
that the Company shall pay to the Employee: (i) any portion of the Employee&rsquo;s Base Salary for the period up to the date of termination
that has been earned but remains unpaid; and (ii) any benefits that have accrued to the Employee under the terms of the employee benefit
plans of the Company, which benefits shall be paid in accordance with the terms of those plans.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 1in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>


